# A Map or Set of hashing keys (Int, String) removes by moving its last
# entry into the gap (BuildMaps ir_map_close_gap), so a removal shifts no
# entries and renumbers no index. The program removes 150,000 of 300,000 Int
# keys and a third of 100,000 String keys and Set members; shifting the later
# entries and renumbering the whole index on each removal would move about
# 10^11 words, so finishing under each step's timeout proves removal does
# not. Ordered reads still see ascending keys after removals from the sorted
# entries and the tail, a moved key is still found, and a Rank keeps its
# order.
fixture: MapRemovesByHashInConstantTime.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet run -O0 main.jet
timeout: 60s
exit: 0
stdout: = map_removes_by_hash_in_constant_time.out
step: jet run -O1 main.jet
timeout: 60s
exit: 0
stdout: = map_removes_by_hash_in_constant_time.out
step: jet run -O2 main.jet
timeout: 60s
exit: 0
stdout: = map_removes_by_hash_in_constant_time.out
step: jet build main.jet
timeout: 120s
exit: 0
step: .jet/build/main
timeout: 60s
exit: 0
stdout: = map_removes_by_hash_in_constant_time.out
